Just FYI, the PSCommand API is designed to support the builder pattern so you can save some boilerplate here:

```csharp
    powerShell.AddCommand("Export-PSSession")
        .AddParameter("OutputModule", wildcardEscapedPath)
        .AddParameter("Module", remoteModuleName)
        .AddParameter("FormatTypeName", "*")
        .AddParameter("Force");

    if (!importModuleOptions.NoClobberExportPSSession)
    {
        powerShell.AddParameter("AllowClobber");
    }
```

(Also `AddParameter()` with a single argument adds a switch parameter)

